From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:42:22 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ngp-carts

Neo Geo Pocket and Pocket Color carts are drawn as an NGP pak in the
retro bitmap renderer (ADR 0054): a ridged cap a little wider than the
body, the wide label (246x133 on the 312x268 pak) in a recessed frame,
and below a seam two plaques with a down arrow between them, pressed in.
Both take the dark grey shell 0x24 0x25 0x29 by the maintainer's choice;
a shell colour chosen in Config/cart_shell.txt still wins. The pak seats
at 240x206 on the shelf, and the label fetcher's art fills the well.

The pak's proportions, label panel, cap grooves, seam, plaques and arrow
and the grey are from nelynes/slotPlus a8eae4c (assets/src/carts.py
neogeo_pocket, slot-ui shell.rs NGP_SHELL; GPL-3.0), redrawn as our own
outline and relief SVGs; the plaque lettering is left out. The neutral
PNG comes from examples/retro_neutrals.rs, whose disc seed is now the
literal it already was, so every other neutral regenerates byte for byte.
